# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to
# the app, and inlines them at BUILD time — a production build carries whatever
# was set when it was built, so rebuild after changing any of these.

# ── Mocking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When true (the default), the dev server answers every API route itself and
# VITE_API_URL below is ignored entirely. Set to false to hit the real service.
# Leaving it unset means mocked, on purpose: an accidental real submission to a
# government service is much worse than an accidental mock.
VITE_USE_MOCK=true

# ── API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The base URL of the service: scheme and host, no trailing slash, no path.
# One variable, because every call goes to the same place.
#
# The paths and methods are NOT configuration — they live in code, in
# src/lib/endpoints.ts, which is also what both mocks route on:
#
#   GET {VITE_API_URL}/protocolo?protocoloId=<15 digits>   ->  { "id": "..." }
#   PUT {VITE_API_URL}/protocolo/protocolaragendamento/<id>
#   PUT {VITE_API_URL}/protocolo/protocolaragendamentoas/<id>
#
# Leave EMPTY to call the app's own origin, which is what you want when routing
# through the Vite dev proxy (see vite.config.ts) to dodge CORS. An absolute
# https:// URL also works if the service sends CORS headers.
#
# Ignored while VITE_USE_MOCK=true: the base is forced to the app's own origin
# so that mocking cannot be silently bypassed. See src/lib/config.ts.
VITE_API_URL=

# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request. Leave empty and no
# Authorization header is sent at all.
#
# This is NOT a secret once built: Vite inlines it into the JS bundle, so anyone
# with the app can read it. Fine for a token issued to this app on a controlled
# device — if it must not leave the server, leave this empty and have the proxy
# in vite.config.ts add the header instead.
#
# When set and VITE_USE_MOCK=true, the mock demands this exact token and answers
# 401 otherwise, so a broken wiring fails in dev instead of in production.
VITE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-request timeout in milliseconds.
VITE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
